{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_chapter12b", "label": "Chapter 12B \u2014 The tower, \u039b\u2089 to \u039b\u2081\u2083", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_ninth_axis_composition", "label": "The ninth axis makes transitions compose", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u039b\u2088 cannot be iterated because its target has three coordinates and its source four; supplying the target's multiplicity makes every target a legal source."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_lambda9_category", "label": "\u039b\u2089 is a category of transitions \u2014 41,682 composable pairs, zero failures, associative", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_composability_grading", "label": "Three gradings, not two \u2014 composability is lost one step before exactness", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "v is a counting coordinate that closes exactly and yet has no source counterpart, so an axis can be exact and not composable; none is composable and not exact."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_axis_table", "label": "The five tower axes \u2014 2S\u2032, v, 2J_c, K, 2J with their bounds, cells and densities", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_tree_or_tightness", "label": "The tree or the tightness \u2014 1,561 cells against 1,654", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A tighter spin bound closes, but only by giving the constraint graph its first cycle, so the language offers both only up to that trade."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_three_excluded_forms", "label": "Three excluded constraint forms \u2014 sums, differences, and symmetric bounds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The exact ceiling of every coupling axis is symmetric under particle-hole conjugation, and a symmetric non-constant function is not monotone, so the admissible form cannot carry it."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_envelope_machines", "label": "The envelope gap's three machines \u2014 reflection, congruence, triangle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_dichotomy", "label": "The dichotomy \u2014 counting coordinates close exactly, coupling coordinates close as envelopes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The price of certainty is not paid once at the door; it is paid per coupling axis. And the surplus is not waste: every envelope cell is a tripwire."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_law_vs_extent", "label": "A bound from the law, or a bound from the extent", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u211b builds its bounds from a set's own projections, so it is an extent-bound operator throughout; E(X) is therefore the price of describing a set by its extent rather than by its law, and E(X) = 0 says the extent IS the law for that set."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_path_dependence", "label": "Precision is path-dependent; physics is not \u2014 64.4% through K against 39.4% direct", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recoupling holds for the exact J-set, but the envelope does not commute with it: the index remembers the route, the atom does not."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_k_boundary_two_parents", "label": "The boundary \u2014 the exact K bound has two parents, one on each side of the cylinder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is the first bridge between the cylinder's two ends other than q and breaks factorisation by 15,150 cells at \u039b\u2081\u2082; the book takes the one-parent form, preserving the tree and the cylinder at the cost of admitting a little more than the law does."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_e1_false_prediction", "label": "An index whose one prediction is false \u2014 the E1 selection rule", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "E(X) counts proposals, not guarantees: here the single proposal is known false, vetoed by structure the index does not carry, which is the method reporting precisely the one thing it cannot see."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_figure_12_4", "label": "Figure 12.4 \u2014 the constraint tree of the full tower", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_figure_12_5", "label": "Figure 12.5 \u2014 the solid in silhouette, \u039b\u2081\u2083 against \u039b\u2088", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_chapter12b", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_ninth_axis_composition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_chapter12b", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12b_tower_lambda9_category", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12B-tower.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "